ppen  and if you don't try that's at least  one outcome that's been decided  that's great advice thank you so much  sarah really appreciate you joining us  yeah thank you bye  so next time you see someone not getting  the credit they deserve  do them justice and don't forget to stay  kind  that's my favorite part joining us now  in the studio are steve and his favorite  son that would be emmett his favorite  daughter that would be merrill emmett is  12 and meryl is eight welcome hartman  family mom andreas over there taking  pictures welcome andrea good to see you  too steve why don't you start not steve  emma why don't you start us off what  inspired you about about so i think it's  i think it's amazing that one  girl can take the initiative noticing  that someone doesn't have enough  recognition and then ending up  naming a school yeah that she's paying  attention when most kids aren't even  paying attention about that merrell  number one you look lovely i like the  blazer i love how look how merrell's  sitting it's just professional i like it  meryl and i like how you always end  every segment with staycon you should  see me in the studio every day every  time you're on i go i wait wait for that  she loves it i love i do i really love  it we all do why did you why why do you  like ending your segments with that well  i think it's just really important it's  like a responsibility like if you don't  do it you're not you you're not complete  and steve i guess we should throw a  question your way as well since you're  here if we have to  yes since you're here  we'll drive them  what's the best part of doing this with  your kids  you know kindness is something and all  the things we talk about we all need  reminders it's not something you learn  once and you're done with it and i think  it's great doing it with my kids because  although these lessons do sink in they  do need reminders they're typical kids  and the adults watching i think need  reminders too so it's good to be you  know doing this over and over because  you know it takes a while to sink in  yeah you can't just do it it's not a one  not a one-time thing right that's why i  encourage people to watch these over and  over yes yes and speaking of watching  these over and over emmitt or merrill  you can take this what does it feel like  to know that these videos these clips  are being shown in classrooms around the  country maybe even around the world  well  i feel like it's just amazing to see  that someone listens someone knows  that  you're doing something and that it makes  a difference in the world yeah but it's  quite a powerful thing you're over there  on the dictionary desk and your words  are going all around the world yeah it's  definitely nice to know that other  people are listening i feel that too you  know steve i get stopped on the street  by teachers mostly but sometimes adults  but mostly teachers who say how can i  get this in my classroom i love what you  guys are doing it's so needed in the  world you must be getting this if i'm  getting stopped i know you must be  getting no we found sort of we found  just by accident almost that tens of  thousands of teachers around the country  around the world are using the stories  we have a facebook group kindness 101  where teachers can  share lesson plans and and which stories  work to teach with which lessons so we  encourage teachers to join that group  steve i've worked with my daughter and  every time i've done things with her i  learn more about her um what have you  learned about your kids during this  process i've learned that they are much  deeper thinkers than i probably gave  them credit for originally  and that i'm learning as much from them  as they are from me i think sometimes we  think of adults as the teachers but  really you know the kids can teach us a  lot too that's really good and working  with your dad what's it like  emmett in 30 seconds or less uh in 30  seconds or less  it's nice he'